One more question , I don't know whether it is a proper place to discuss here. Abstract class service can be a DI params, such as :
```
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export abstract class AbstractService {
}

export class AppComponent {
  constructor(private service: AbstractService) {
  }
}
```
As you can see , I inject a abstract service into a component. At now, Angular won't throw error with this usage.
In my opinion, we cannot inject a abstract class service, because we cannot create a instance of abstract class. 
I am not sure this is working as intended or a bug.

